{
  "manufacturer": "Fireye",
  "manufacturer_slug": "fireye",
  "model": "PPC4000 parallel positioning burner control (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "ppc4000",
  "short_model": "PPC4000",
  "aliases": [
    "PPC-4000",
    "PPC4000",
    "MOD-4001"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler (burner management / fuel-air ratio control)",
  "applies_to": "Fireye PPC4000 parallel positioning controls showing engineering code EC08 or later, per bulletin MOD-4001 (September 13, 2012). The later NXF4000 is not covered.",
  "summary": "The PPC4000 is Fireye's parallel positioning fuel/air ratio control for burners. It is a Modbus RTU slave with holding registers only: a read-only block of status, counters, positions, raw sensor values and lockout history, and a small read/write block for burner on/off, low fire, lead/lag, auto/manual and manual modulation rate.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The bulletin prints holding register numbers from 40001 next to the message address actually sent (40001 = address 00, 41002 = 1001). Subtract 40001 for the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Engineering code EC08 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "PPC4000 Modbus Communications",
    "doc_number": "MOD-4001",
    "revision_date": "2012-09-13",
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/MOD-4001.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 1 (protocol), pp. 2-7 (register tables, raw sensor conversion)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Fireye's own copy of this bulletin was not reachable (the later MOD-4001-NXF4000_PPC4000 link on fireye.com returns 404); this copy is served by a controls distributor and is the unaltered Fireye bulletin.",
    "The three 32-bit counters are listed as an upper-16-bit register followed by a lower-16-bit register, so they read as ABCD UINT32.",
    "VFD positions are 0-1000 in tenths of a degree, so scale 0.1 gives degrees; servo positions and set point/alarm values have no stated scaling and are raw.",
    "Raw sensor conversion from the bulletin: value = ((raw / calibration constant - 0.2) / 0.8) * range + offset, using 40052 as the calibration constant and the range/offset of the fitted sensor (e.g. TS350: range 318, offset 32). Sensors 4 and 5 are raw only.",
    "Lockout history: only fault 1 (most recent) is listed; faults 2-10 follow at 40200-40253 in six-register groups with the same layout.",
    "O2 probe status and temperature registers (40036-40039) are left out; their meaning is in the separate O2 probe manual.",
    "Error codes are listed in a separate Fireye publication; this bulletin does not explain the operational state numbers 0-16."
  ],
